.TH scrollreversed 1 2026-11-03 "scrollreversed 0.1.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
scrollreversed \- Darwin daemon reversing mouse or trackpad scrolling
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscrollreversed\fR [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-axis\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
scrollreversed reverses the scroll direction of either the mouse or the trackpad, so that each can scroll its own way despite the single natural scrolling setting in System Settings.
.PP
Settings come from the configuration file described in scrollreversed(5).  Options given on the command line override them.
.PP
The device behind each scroll event is looked up in the I/O Registry and classified the way Darwin picks between the Mouse and Trackpad scroll settings, so a Magic Mouse counts as a mouse.  Events whose sender is not in the registry, such as events posted by other applications or forwarded by Universal Control, are classified by gesture phase instead.
.PP
The process needs Accessibility access.  Without it, scrollreversed asks for access once and waits until it is granted under System Settings > Privacy & Security > Accessibility.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Device whose scrolling is reversed, overriding the device key of the configuration file [default: mouse]
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
mouse: Mice, including the Magic Mouse
.IP \(bu 2
trackpad: Built\-in and external trackpads
.IP \(bu 2
all: Every device
.RE
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-axis\fR \fI<AXIS>\fR
Axis along which scrolling is reversed, overriding the axis key of the configuration file [default: both]
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
vertical: Vertical scrolling only
.IP \(bu 2
horizontal: Horizontal scrolling only
.IP \(bu 2
both: Both directions
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Log every scroll event and how it was classified to standard error
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read the configuration from PATH, which must exist, instead of $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/scrollreversed/config.toml
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/scrollreversed/config.toml\fR
Configuration file, read at startup.  Without \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fI~/.config\fR takes its place.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBscrollreversed\fR(5), \fBlaunchctl\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
